.TH PLANVIEW 1 "September 2026" "Planview" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
planview \- publish and preview immutable HTML snapshots
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B planview
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B planview help
[\fIcommand\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B planview
publishes an HTML file or page folder to a local daemon and returns a stable
localhost URL. A page folder must contain
.B index.html
and is published with its assets.
.PP
The
.B publish
command creates a snapshot without opening a browser. The
.B preview
command creates the same kind of snapshot and opens its URL in the default
browser.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B publish [options] file|folder
Publish an immutable HTML snapshot and print its URL.
.TP
.B preview [options] file|folder
Publish an immutable HTML snapshot and open its URL in the default browser.
.TP
.B get id|url
Write a stored snapshot's exact bytes to standard output. The reference must be
a document id or an exact local Planview URL.
.TP
.B start [options]
Start the local daemon, or reuse the authenticated daemon already running.
.TP
.B status [options]
Show daemon status without starting a daemon.
.TP
.B stop [options]
Gracefully stop the local daemon.
.TP
.B restart [options]
Restart the local daemon.
.TP
.B clean [options]
Remove expired snapshots and reconcile incomplete storage operations.
.TP
.B skills install [options]
Install the bundled
.B planview
and
.B create-html
Agent Skills into
.B ~/.agents/skills
.
.TP
.B help [command]
Show help for the whole CLI or for one command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show the relevant help text. Use
.B planview help command
to request help explicitly.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show the Planview CLI version.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print one newline-terminated JSON object for metadata commands. Supported by
.B publish
,
.B preview
,
.B start
,
.B status
,
.B stop
,
.B restart
,
and
.B clean
.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Replace existing skill directories when used with
.B skills install
.
.TP
.B \-\-
Stop option parsing. Text after this marker is treated as an operand.
.SH OUTPUT
Successful text output goes to standard output. Errors go to standard error.
.B get
writes only the stored document bytes to standard output.
.PP
With
.B \-\-json
, successful metadata commands write one JSON object followed by a newline.
JSON errors use an
.B error
object on standard error. The
.B get
command does not accept
.B \-\-json
because its output is the stored document itself.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/planview
Default application data directory on supported Unix systems.
.TP
.B ~/.agents/skills
Destination used by
.B skills install
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
The command could not complete, or its arguments were invalid.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
planview publish ./report.html
planview preview ./site
planview get http://localhost:4777/<id> > report.html
planview status --json
planview publish --json ./report.html
planview help publish
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR npm (1),
.BR man (1)
